  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 337 AM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nWarming trend continues after Tuesday with highs on Wednesday \nreaching into the mid to upper 90s for most. Upper level ridging \nmoves over the southern US through the rest of the week with \nsoutherly to southwesterly winds aiding in the warm up and drying\nout. Many areas will see temperatures hit the 100F mark for the \nfirst time since at least earlier this month or late June. Long \nrange guidance keeps the warmth through this coming weekend with \nmuch drier conditions persisting. Overnight low temperatures move\ninto the mid to upper 70s through the week as part of the \nupcoming warming trend.\n\n-Stickney",
